#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572771} :activity/id #uuid "c9f63623-ba17-5baf-a7ac-b373ec69640a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048850 :topic/id #uuid "c60f74c0-bf82-529d-b9dd-b8bfe8e2cc4a" :topic/math-academy-id 1799} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572736 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3103b7b1-e08e-5891-bfbe-c1ec2af0dff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{3}=\\frac{z+5}{4},\\,y=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367242} {:answer/id #uuid "baaea110-f65c-5409-b3a2-13194827514b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{3}=\\frac{z+5}{4},\\,y=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367243} {:answer/id #uuid "6d279abb-4007-52c2-895b-d690c7f724e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{3}=\\frac{z-5}{4},\\,y=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367244} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd346df-59be-5375-8f4c-15f188fbded5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{3}=\\frac{z-5}{4},\\,y=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367245} {:answer/id #uuid "ffcdbe32-6592-5f2a-9fd5-bb2a8ba04aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{3}=\\frac{z-5}{-4},\\,y=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367246}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367244} :answer-field/id #uuid "b609bda9-e776-5fe4-a812-e5bedc6b3f93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "26ccf3a9-18a6-5810-b58b-63343e2dbccc" :question/math-academy-id "q-127534" :question/problem "![](images/f6/f65a9806a2d6736a9eed283253225f6e5405d3e272f25e9c6a763651a19d0a31.png)\n\nFind a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure above." :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-1,2,5)$ and $Q(2,2,9).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,2,9⟩-⟨-1,2,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,0,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-1)}{3}=\\frac{y-2}{0}=\\frac{z-5}{4}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{3}=\\frac{y-2}{0}=\\frac{z-5}{4}.\n$$\n\nBut the above equation is problematic because $\\frac{y-2}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, in our line, the $y$ component always maintains the constant value of $y=2.$ For example, our two points $P(-1,2,5)$ and $Q(2,2,9)$ both have $y$-coordinates of $y=2.$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{y-2}{0}$ part and instead write $y=2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{3}=\\frac{z-5}{4},\\,y=2\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "145ce8df-01ec-57e3-b39c-1ec76660f5ed"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572758 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19e64b37-3c7a-5132-a82c-36330fe10f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{4}=\\frac{y+4}{6}=\\frac{z-5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336271} {:answer/id #uuid "8a752ea7-fe86-5478-aae7-722d6e7a29af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x+4}{3}=\\frac{y+6}{4}=\\frac{z+9}{-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337279} {:answer/id #uuid "a048d6c7-d4d3-50d9-b51c-8fa355607987" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{4}=\\frac{y-4}{6}=\\frac{z+5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337480} {:answer/id #uuid "bf30416c-dc68-5dc0-91dd-21e3d89ecdd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x-4}{3}=\\frac{y-6}{4}=\\frac{z-9}{-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337731} {:answer/id #uuid "df728bc5-3bdf-5b55-bb17-24b6ef4f6f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}=\\frac{y}{6}=\\frac{z}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337982}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337480} :answer-field/id #uuid "32bcf106-ea5d-53fa-a139-89e099b59c67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "db08ec21-5e10-5fa9-a587-34ff723a0e65" :question/math-academy-id "q-71029" :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the vector equation\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." :question/worked-solution "We have the vector equation \n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $P(3,4,-5)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨4,6,9⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{4}=\\frac{y-4}{6}=\\frac{z-(-5)}{9}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{4}=\\frac{y-4}{6}=\\frac{z+5}{9}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "40a8a766-a5ff-53c3-a1e8-af197b8d2a13" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572766}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572766 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "212fc367-a57d-5039-af89-08026c3e410f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y+2}{5}=\\frac{z+4}{7},\\,x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572362} {:answer/id #uuid "9050e322-04a0-5d40-9058-40462def8edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y+2}{5}=\\frac{z-4}{7},\\,x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572470} {:answer/id #uuid "a0ce538d-74d3-56e8-9c99-e8c37ca44578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y-2}{5}=\\frac{z-4}{7},\\,x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572488} {:answer/id #uuid "a8ed6ee6-1a77-5ed5-81ec-29a7a1f2a89e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y-2}{7}=\\frac{z-4}{5},\\,x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572496} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd0c658-006c-55c8-a0a8-ba8100080481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{1}=\\frac{z-4}{7},\\,y=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572574}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572488} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7fb6b07-3aa3-5e0b-beb1-701386482c7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3f6ecd28-8af0-5770-801c-e2211846f047" :question/math-academy-id "q-127457" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-1)}{0}=\\frac{y-2}{5}=\\frac{z-4}{7}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{0}=\\frac{y-2}{5}=\\frac{z-4}{7},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{x+1}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $x$ component always maintains the constant value of $x=-1:$\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2+5t \\\\ 4+7t\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{x+1}{0}$ part and instead write $x=-1$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{y-2}{5}=\\frac{z-4}{7},\\,x=-1\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "57929708-6e1f-5624-b944-a9831f7009b2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572736}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572771 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120506 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a901e00-4252-5cf9-b50c-8893fcb829e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119151} {:answer/id #uuid "abbd4785-c8dc-50a2-be07-f1eb6893222e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x = \\frac{y - 2}{1}, z =-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119152} {:answer/id #uuid "e119e113-a4c0-584f-9f11-17fe5d0b1a7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x = \\frac{y - 1}{2} =-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119153} {:answer/id #uuid "71528ca6-7a70-59a0-9b5d-8a8f4816dab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y - 1}{2} =-z, x =-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119154} {:answer/id #uuid "7a38b494-2053-5910-85da-23542283aa10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x + 1 = \\frac{y - 1}{2} =-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119155}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2f354396-1623-5d78-92fe-a7def331ac1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f348ab2b-70ba-5d55-a038-1c2b971bae5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368670} {:answer/id #uuid "4b489027-ff1d-5463-ab8c-dd167ba0d700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x=\\frac{y-2}{1},\\,z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368671} {:answer/id #uuid "610d18c7-3941-5814-b7ec-e0be41696393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y-1}{2}=-z,\\,x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368672} {:answer/id #uuid "7c80d818-a51e-5a06-9a27-142460430c64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+1=\\frac{y-1}{2}=-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368673} {:answer/id #uuid "4405ea39-6ccf-5364-9088-7dbb9d9a5f38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=\\frac{y-1}{2}=-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368674}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368672} :answer-field/id #uuid "adf6930c-774a-5b1f-b8be-4a33d604e6b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9ba33a02-c52b-5c65-80c6-40fc93de31d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-70641" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-1)}{0}=\\frac{y-1}{2}=\\frac{z-0}{-1}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{0}=\\frac{y-1}{2}=-z,\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{x+1}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $x$ component always maintains the constant value of $x=-1:$\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1+2t \\\\ -t\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{x+1}{0}$ part and instead write $x=-1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{y-1}{2}=-z,\\,x=-1\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "72290fe9-7f75-5e81-8a56-0f0853a90f24" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572793}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572793 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572698 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dcb7205-b034-5093-9cf9-80e20c097a91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y+2}{-3}=\\frac{z-7}{4},\\,x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572428} {:answer/id #uuid "69cd5697-9cbd-58ff-a0e3-84ea330a8135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y-2}{-3}=\\frac{z+7}{4},\\,x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572439} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed64ac1-d5c4-5bf3-848a-0de3f90725b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{-1}=\\frac{y+3}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572468} {:answer/id #uuid "b37bf921-f834-5009-a13c-c6f81e68b8b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{-1}=\\frac{y}{-2}=\\frac{z}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572516} {:answer/id #uuid "c75ca808-618d-5710-b5d0-4804627d2e41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{-1}=\\frac{y-3}{-2}=\\frac{z+4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572539}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572468} :answer-field/id #uuid "19df2e81-2346-53c6-b28c-0f1afc312307" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7e38002f-06be-5b6a-8718-39abfb36add8" :question/math-academy-id "q-71022" :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the parametric equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-t \\\\ y &=-3-2t \\\\ z &=4+7t\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-t \\\\ -3-2t \\\\ 4+7t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-t \\\\ -2t \\\\ 7t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThis implies that the given line passes through the point $P(0,-3,4)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-1,-2,7⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-0}{-1}=\\frac{y-(-3)}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{7}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{-1}=\\frac{y+3}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{7}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "be45a931-3267-5e9b-af10-acc0bc85bcf2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572758}}] :activity/title "The Cartesian Equation of a Line" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572311}]}
